maya: Heads-up: we're removing the v1 webhook shim next month. The migration guide currently has an old example that POSTs raw JSON to /v1/webhooks. Need a short migration section showing the v2 signed webhook format and a tiny listener example for Express and Flask. Also include a fallback header `X-Redwood-Compat: webhook=v1` that customers can opt into for 30 days.

juan: Agreed. I saw a customer report where their webhook handler failed silently because the signature header name changed from `X-RW-Sig` to `RW-Signature`. We should call that out clearly and show verification snippets.

frank: Draft Express snippet for PR: 
```js
// v2 webhook verification (node/express)
import crypto from 'crypto';
app.post('/webhook', express.raw({type: 'application/json'}), (req, res) => {
  const sig = req.get('RW-Signature');
  const expected = crypto.createHmac('sha256', process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET)
    .update(req.body).digest('hex');
  if (!sig || !crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(sig), Buffer.from(expected))) {
    return res.status(401).send('invalid signature');
  }
  const payload = JSON.parse(req.body.toString());
  // handle event
  res.sendStatus(200);
});
```

maya: Nice. Can you also paste a short Flask example for Python? Support prefers both.

juan: Python snippet (Flask):
```py
# v2 webhook verification (python/flask)
from flask import Flask, request, abort
import hmac, hashlib, os

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/webhook', methods=['POST'])
def webhook():
    sig = request.headers.get('RW-Signature')
    body = request.get_data()
    expected = hmac.new(os.environ['WEBHOOK_SECRET'].encode(), body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
    if not sig or not hmac.compare_digest(sig, expected):
        abort(401)
    event = request.get_json()
    # handle event
    return ('', 204)
```

